  "summary": "The `projects.locations.collections.dataconnector.mcp` method in Discovery Engine has a significant breaking change to its URI path and parameter structure. Additionally, new observability and project provisioning options are available.",
  "details": "The `projects.locations.collections.dataconnector.mcp` method has undergone a major breaking change. Its URI path template has changed from `v1/projects/{projectsId}/locations/{locationsId}/collections/{collectionsId}/dataConnector/mcp` to a consolidated `v1/{+name}/mcp`. This means the individual `projectsId`, `locationsId`, and `collectionsId` parameters have been removed and are now part of a single, required `name` parameter. This `name` parameter expects a full resource path in the format `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/collections/{collection}/dataConnector`. Furthermore, the `contentType`, `data`, and `extensions` parameters, previously top-level, are now nested within a new `httpBody` object. Your code calling this method will need immediate updates.\n\nIn addition to these breaking changes, the API introduces new capabilities. `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1alphaObservabilityConfig` now includes `artifactGcsBucket` (string) to specify a Cloud Storage bucket for agent artifacts and `userPrincipalLoggingEnabled` (boolean) to enable logging of user identities even when sensitive logging is off. For project provisioning, `GoogleCloudDiscoveryengineV1ProvisionProjectRequest` gains a new `preProvisionMode` (boolean) parameter. When set to `true`, this allows running common project-level pre-provisioning steps without interacting with customer, collection, or user store tables, useful for initial setup.",
